@page "/admin/spells"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using Faolan.Core.Enums
@inherits AdminDbPage

<PageTitle>Spells — Admin</PageTitle>

<div class="se">
	<div class="se-head">
		<h1>Spell editor</h1>
		<span class="warn">⚠ edits the live game DB — restart the server to pick up changes</span>
	</div>

	@if (!Authorized)
	{
		<p class="muted">Checking access…</p>
	}
	else
	{
		@if (Status != null)
		{
			<p class="se-status @(Error
				                    ? "err"
				                    : "")">
				@Status
			</p>
		}

		<div class="se-grid">
			<aside class="se-list">
				<input class="filter" placeholder="Filter by id / name…" @bind="Filter" @bind:event="oninput"/>
				<label class="onlyfx">
					<input type="checkbox" @bind="_onlyWithEffects"/> only spells with effects
				</label>
				<div class="rowlist">
					@foreach (var s in Filtered())
					{
						<button class="@(ReferenceEquals(s, _spell)
							               ? "sel"
							               : "")" @onclick="() => Select(s)">
							<span class="sid">@s.Id</span>
							<span class="sname">@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(s.Name)
								                     ? "(unnamed)"
								                     : s.Name)</span>
							@if (EffectCount(s.Id) is > 0 and var fx)
							{
								<span class="badge fx">@fx fx</span>
							}
							@if (StatEffectCount(s.Id) is > 0 and var sfx)
							{
								<span class="badge sfx">@sfx stat</span>
							}
						</button>
					}
				</div>
				<span class="count">@_shown of @_spells.Count</span>
			</aside>

			<section class="se-detail">
				@if (_spell == null)
				{
					<p class="muted">Select a spell.</p>
				}
				else
				{
					<div class="se-fields">
						<label>Id<input value="@_spell.Id" disabled/></label>
						<label>Name<input @bind="_spell.Name"/></label>
						<label>Level<input class="n" @bind="_spell.Level"/></label>
						<label title="RDB field 123, carried RAW. The rank for MOST spells but not all: measured over the 883 spells whose name also carries a &quot;(Rank N)&quot; suffix, 669 agree and 214 are a clean rank × 10. The scale differs by spell FAMILY, so do not read this as a rank without checking.">
							Rank (raw)<input class="n" @bind="_spell.Rank"/>
						</label>
						<label title="milliseconds — RDB field 0x126 × 10">Cast time (ms)<input class="n" @bind="_spell.CastTime"/></label>
						<label title="SECONDS, not ms — matches the source that carries it">Cooldown (s)<input class="n" @bind="_spell.Cooldown"/></label>
						<label>Mana cost<input class="n" @bind="_spell.ManaCost"/></label>
						<label title="metres — RDB field 0x11F / 100">Range (m)<input class="n" @bind="_spell.Range"/></label>
						<label title="percent — RDB field 0x15C / 100">Damage rating<input class="n" @bind="_spell.DamageRating"/></label>
						<label title="0 = no self-duration. Drives buff expiry: a timed self-buff gets its end-twin sent at 0 so the icon disappears.">
							Duration (ms)<input class="n" @bind="_spell.DurationMs"/>
						</label>
						<label title="per-tick HealthCurrent delta while the debuff is active; negative = a bleed">DoT delta<input class="n" @bind="_spell.DotDelta"/></label>
						<label title="the +45 damage-school flag carried into the rebuilt StatDamageIIR">DoT type<input class="n" @bind="_spell.DotType"/></label>
						<label title="gap between DoT ticks, measured from captured StatDamageIIR records (500 ms … 11 s). 0 = unmeasured, and the world tick falls back to the old 2 s constant — which is right for the Incinerate family and wrong everywhere else.">
							DoT interval (ms)<input class="n" @bind="_spell.DotIntervalMs"/>
						</label>
						<label>Effect spell<input class="n" @bind="_spell.EffectSpell"/></label>
					</div>

					@if (_spell.DotDelta != 0 && _spell.DotIntervalMs == 0)
					{
						<p class="chainhint warnhint">
							This spell is a DoT (<b>DoT delta @_spell.DotDelta</b>) with <b>no measured tick interval</b>, so the world
							tick runs it at the fallback 2 s. That is right for the Incinerate family and wrong for most others.
						</p>
					}

					@if (_spell.DurationMs == 0 && StatEffectCount(_spell.Id) > 0)
					{
						<p class="chainhint warnhint">
							This spell carries stat effects but <b>no duration</b>, so it is applied as an INSTANT and never tracked —
							nothing will ever expire it or send its removal twin. If the client renders an icon for it, that icon sticks.
						</p>
					}

					<div class="se-fx-head">
						<h2>Server-acted effects</h2>
						<button class="add" @onclick="AddEffect">+ Add effect</button>
					</div>
					<div class="tablewrap">
						<table class="se-fx">
							<thead>
							<tr>
								<th title="WHEN it fires. OnCast = this spell is cast. OnFatality = a fatality lands while this spell is a LIVE buff on the killer.">Trigger</th>
								<th title="run order within one (spell, trigger)">Seq</th>
								<th title="WHAT it does — each kind reads a different subset of the columns">Kind</th>
								<th title="ApplySpell: the BASE id of the spell to apply">TargetSpellId</th>
								<th title="SummonPet: the creature TYPE name (NpcTemplate.Name)">Template</th>
								<th title="SummonPet: combat pet (targetable, takes commands) vs social companion">Combat</th>
								<th title="SummonPet: pet lifetime. Empty = until dismissed.">Duration (ms)</th>
								<th title="SummonPet: ceiling a re-summon may extend a timed pet to">Max duration (ms)</th>
								<th></th>
							</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
							@foreach (var fx in Effects())
							{
								<tr>
									<td>
										<select @bind="fx.Trigger">
											@foreach (var t in Triggers)
											{
												<option value="@t">@t</option>
											}
										</select>
									</td>
									<td>
										<input class="n" @bind="fx.Sequence"/>
									</td>
									<td>
										<select @bind="fx.Kind">
											@foreach (var k in Kinds)
											{
												<option value="@k">@k</option>
											}
										</select>
									</td>
									<td>
										<input class="n" @bind="fx.TargetSpellId" placeholder="—" disabled="@(fx.Kind != SpellEffectKind.ApplySpell)"/>
									</td>
									<td>
										<input @bind="fx.Template" placeholder="—" disabled="@(fx.Kind != SpellEffectKind.SummonPet)"/>
									</td>
									<td>
										<input type="checkbox" @bind="fx.Combat" disabled="@(fx.Kind != SpellEffectKind.SummonPet)"/>
									</td>
									<td>
										<input class="n" @bind="fx.DurationMs" placeholder="∞" disabled="@(fx.Kind != SpellEffectKind.SummonPet)"/>
									</td>
									<td>
										<input class="n" @bind="fx.MaxDurationMs" placeholder="—" disabled="@(fx.Kind != SpellEffectKind.SummonPet)"/>
									</td>
									<td>
										<button class="del" title="Remove effect" @onclick="() => RemoveEffect(fx)">✕</button>
									</td>
								</tr>
							}
							@if (!Effects().Any())
							{
								<tr>
									<td colspan="9" class="empty">No server-acted effects — this spell resolves through the generic wire path.</td>
								</tr>
							}
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</div>
					<p class="hint">
						These are the effects the server has to act on ITSELF, as data rather than an id hardcoded into a dispatch
						chain: a pet summon, or a proc armed on a later event. The generic path (ApplySpell + the duration above +
						the stat deltas below) already covers a buff that only modifies its carrier, so most spells need no row here.
					</p>

					<div class="se-fx-head">
						<h2>Stat effects <span class="ro">read-only</span></h2>
					</div>
					<div class="tablewrap">
						<table class="se-fx statfx">
							<thead>
							<tr>
								<th>Stat</th>
								<th title="the ~53000-range word that opens the template record — flat vs percent vs health">Effect kind</th>
								<th title="RAW template value; the scale is PER-STAT and is not the item scale">Amount (raw)</th>
							</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
							@foreach (var sfx in StatEffects())
							{
								<tr>
									<td>@sfx.StatId (0x@(((uint)sfx.StatId).ToString("X")))</td>
									<td>@sfx.EffectKind</td>
									<td class="n">@sfx.Amount</td>
								</tr>
							}
							@if (!StatEffects().Any())
							{
								<tr>
									<td colspan="3" class="empty">No stat effects extracted for this spell.</td>
								</tr>
							}
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</div>
					<p class="hint">
						Deliberately NOT editable: this table is the client's own <code>[2][9]</code> template region, machine-extracted
						per spell and re-derived wholesale on every RDB re-import — an edit here would be silently overwritten by the
						next import. It is shown because it is what a buff actually modifies. Its <b>Amount</b> scale is per-stat and is
						<i>not</i> the item scale (attributes store display units, movement/percentage stats store large scaled
						magnitudes), which is why the server honours only what it can justify.
					</p>

					<div class="se-actions">
						<button class="save" @onclick="Save">Save</button>
					</div>
				}
			</section>
		</div>
	}
</div>
